### 12. Explain AOP and its use cases.

**Answer:**
AOP (Aspect-Oriented Programming) is used for separating cross-cutting concerns like logging, transactions, and security.

Example:

```java
@Aspect
@Component
public class LoggingAspect {
    @Before("execution(* com.example.employee.service.*.*(..))")
    public void logBefore(JoinPoint jp) {
        System.out.println("Executing: " + jp.getSignature());
    }
}
```

**Use cases:** Logging, performance tracking, transaction management.

